<!--
========================================================================
 Unit_Test_Procedure_Round_4.xml
 No-parameter procedure test.
 Exercises the zero-param code path in build_plsql_block which
 generates:  BEGIN proc_name; END;
 Useful for maintenance procedures (purge, refresh, etc.)

 Example Oracle procedure this test targets:
 CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE DATA_MANAGER.PURGE_OLD_ROWS AS
 BEGIN
     DELETE FROM DATA_MANAGER.OCI_FIELD_TEST
     WHERE  DATE_COL < SYSDATE - 365;
     COMMIT;
 END;

 Expected log markers:
   PL/SQL block: BEGIN DATA_MANAGER.PURGE_OLD_ROWS; END;
   PL/SQL execute OK elapsed=...
   execute_procedure complete

 New request-envelope format per Data_Manager_Request_Definitions.docx.
 <parameters> stays present but empty - level2_validate_procedure()
 correctly treats param_count=0 as valid (a procedure may take none),
 not a validation failure.

 2026-07-31 fix: removed an invalid hyphen-run comment separator - see
 Round 1's own fixture for the full explanation.
========================================================================
-->

<request version="1.0">
    <external_audit_id>audit_stub_procedure_round_4</external_audit_id>
    <session_id>-</session_id>
    <transaction required="1">
        <operation type="EXECUTE_PROCEDURE">
            <procedure_name>PURGE_OLD_ROWS</procedure_name>
            <owner>DATA_MANAGER</owner>
            <parameters>
            </parameters>
        </operation>
    </transaction>
</request>
